gbeR(){return"Which ornament is on the note?"},
gbeS(){return"Trill"},
gbeQ(){return"Mordent"},
gbeT(){return"Turn"},
gbiR(){return"On the beat, or off?"},
gbiQ(){return"Usually the notes land right ON the beats \u2014 count 1-2-3-4 and each note lands on a number. Steady and square."},
gbiP(){return'Syncopation pushes notes OFF the beat, onto the "and" in between. The accent lands where your ear didnt expect it \u2014 thats the kick you feel in pop and jazz.'},
gbjc(){return"Two or three in a beat"},
gbja(){return'Normally a beat splits into TWO even halves: "1-and". Two eighth notes.'},
gbjb(){return'A triplet squeezes THREE equal notes into that same beat: "trip-o-let". It gets a little 3 above it.'},
gbi6(){return"Decorating a note"},
gbi7(){return"Ornaments are little signs that dress up a note. A trill (tr) shakes quickly between the note and the one just above it."},
gbi8(){return"A turn (a sideways S) curls AROUND the note: the note above, the note, the note below, then back. A mordent is just one quick flick up and back."},
ga5y(){return"Label the Form"},
gatu(){return"Hear the sections; name the shape (ABA\u2026)"},
gb44(){return"What is the form? (same colour = same tune)"},
gb43(){return"Listen"},
gbha(){return"The shape of a piece"},
gbh9(){return"Music is built from sections. Here is a little tune \u2014 call it section A. Whenever it comes back, it is A again."},
gbh8(){return"A different tune is a new letter \u2014 section B. Tune, different tune, then the first tune again makes the form A-B-A. Lots of songs are shaped this way!"},
ga6_(){return"Which Mode?"},
gatW(){return"Major, minor or Dorian?"},
gbcH(){return"Listen! Which mode is it?"},
ga2z(){return"Major"},
ga2A(){return"Minor"},
gbcG(){return"Dorian"},
gbi2(){return"Three colours of scale"},
gbi0(){return"A major scale sounds bright and happy. Listen to it climb."},
gbi1(){return"A minor scale sounds darker \u2014 its 3rd, 6th and 7th steps sit a little lower."},
gbi_(){return"Dorian is like minor, but its 6th step is raised \u2014 so it sounds minor with a brighter twist. That one note is the whole secret!"},
gapL(){return"Textbook"},
gbof(){return"Read"},
gboc(){return"Work through music from the very start. Each topic has a short lesson (see it, hear it) and games to practise it."},
gbo6(){return"Lesson coming soon"},
gboe(){return"Read the lesson"},
gbod(){return"Practise"},
galj(){return"See the form"},
gali(){return"Play the whole piece"},
gb3V(){return"Tap a block to hear that section."},
galG(){return"See the harmony"},
gb5_(){return"Tap a chord to hear it."},
gPZ(){return"Home (tonic)"},
gPY(){return"Away (subdominant)"},
gPX(){return"Tension (dominant)"},
gb4m(){return"Home"},
gb4l(){return"Away"},
gb4k(){return"Tension"},
gaRH(){return"Harmony"},
gaRR(){return"Analyse the harmony"},
gDe(){return"Inspect (tap a note)"},
gaRG(){return"Form"},
gaRC(){return"Circle of fifths"},
gaRP(){return"Tension"},
gahD(){return"Voice leading"},
gaRQ(){return"No parallel 5ths or 8ves \u2713"},
gaRN(){return"Parallel fifths"},
gaRO(){return"Parallel octaves"},
gahC(){return"Non-chord tones"},
gaij(){return"perfect cadence"},
gail(){return"half cadence"},
gaim(){return"plagal cadence"},
gaik(){return"deceptive cadence"},
